    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it just feels so exhausting, honestly. when you put it like that—that staying alive is just a \"default setting\" or a lack of agency—it makes everything feel so pointless. if the only \"authentic\" thing I can do is walk away, then everything I'm doing right now, trying to build a life or find a reason to keep going, just feels like I'm being a coward or playing a part in a lie. it's almost like there's no dignity in just continuing to struggle when the exit is right there.",
